      "content": "I truly understand how distressing this situation is and your urgency to help your son. However, administering multiple puffs outside of the recommended dosage is not typically safe and can lead to serious side effects, such as worsening symptoms or severe reactions. While a doctor in an ER might administer higher doses in some cases, it's done under strict monitoring and usually after other interventions failed.\n\nA higher dose is not advisable for someone not in a medical setting. It's critical to monitor his symptoms after each puff and be vigilant for signs of adverse effects, but the emergency medical team will refer to the latest guidelines and his medical history to determine the appropriate dosage. Trying to titrate his medication yourself bypasses the precautions that potentially lifesaving procedures are covered under.\n\nI strongly recommend calling emergency services now. They are trained for such acute situations and can help you figure out the safest and fastest way to help your child.",
